    "text": "To determine the total number of fishes caught by Jackson, Jonah, and George over the 5-day Fishing competition, we need to calculate the number of fishes each person caught and then sum these amounts.\n\nFirst, let's calculate the number of fishes Jackson caught:\nJackson catches 6 fishes per day. Over 5 days, the total number of fishes Jackson caught is:\n\\[ 6 \\text{ fishes/day} \\times 5 \\text{ days} = 30 \\text{ fishes} \\]\n\nNext, let's calculate the number of fishes Jonah caught:\nJonah catches 4 fishes per day. Over 5 days, the total number of fishes Jonah caught is:\n\\[ 4 \\text{ fishes/day} \\times 5 \\text{ days} = 20 \\text{ fishes} \\]\n\nThen, let's calculate the number of fishes George caught:\nGeorge catches 8 fishes per day. Over 5 days, the total number of fishes George caught is:\n\\[ 8 \\text{ fishes/day} \\times 5 \\text{ days} = 40 \\text{ fishes} \\]\n\nNow, we sum the number of fishes caught by Jackson, Jonah, and George:\n\\[ 30 \\text{ fishes} + 20 \\text{ fishes} + 40 \\text{ fishes} = 90 \\text{ fishes} \\]\n\nTherefore, the total number of fishes they were able to catch throughout the competition is:\n\\[ \\boxed{90} \\]",
